  \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    57→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/15/qr-codes/\",\n    58→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-15\",\n    59→    \"topics\": [\"AI-Assisted Programming\", \"Claude\", \"Tools\", \"QR Codes\"],\n    60→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    61→  },\n    62→  {\n    63→    \"title\": \"Datasette-llm-limits: Per-user spending limits for LLM usage\",\n    64→    \"description\": \"Released a plugin for Datasette that configures per-user or global spending limits for LLM usage, helping control costs. Example shows $1/day per user limit with 24-hour rolling window.\",\n    65→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    66→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    67→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/15/datasette-llm-limits/\",\n    68→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-15\",\n    69→    \"topics\": [\"Datasette\", \"LLMs\", \"Cost Management\", \"Plugins\"],\n    70→    \"type\": \"technical\"\n    71→  },\n    72→  {\n    73→    \"title\": \"Coding agents make programming languages increasingly fungible\",\n    74→    \"description\": \"Discussion of how coding agents have changed the lock-in dynamics of programming languages. Cites example of company using AI to rewrite apps to React Native, and Mitchell Hashimoto's observation about Bun migrating from Zig to Rust. Programming languages used to be LOCK IN, and they're increasingly not so.\",\n    75→    \"author\": \"Simon Willison\",\n    76→    \"source\": \"Blog\",\n    77→    \"url\": \"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/14/programming-languages-fungible/\",\n    78→    \"published_date\": \"2026-05-14\",\n    79→    \"topics\": [\"AI-Assisted Programming\", \"Programming Languages\", \"Coding Agents\", \"React Native\", \"Rust\", \"Zig\"],\n    80→    \"type\": \"opinion\"\n    81→  },\n    82→  {\n    83→    \"title\": \"Rate limiting plugin built with Codex (GPT-5.5 xhigh)\",\n    84→    \"description\": \"Used OpenAI Codex desktop (GPT-5.5 xhigh) to build a configurable ra